.SH "Motivation"
.PP
When visiting the edges of each finite element, this object deals with the accumulation of the fluxes, saturations etc\&. for the transport schemes\&. 
.SH "Constructor & Destructor Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> \fBcsmp::StencilProcessor\fP< dim >::~\fBStencilProcessor\fP ()"
Destructor is used to write theta limiter values (if accumulated) to a text file named "spatial-limiter-values" if the flag write_out_limiter has been set\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> \fBcsmp::StencilProcessor\fP< dim >::StencilProcessor (const \fBStencilProcessor\fP< dim > & tfs)"
Standard assignment operator\&. 
.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::StencilProcessor\fP< dim >::AccumulateImplicitTwoPhaseSolution1 (const \fBFV_Parameter\fP & param, const \fBElement\fP< dim > & e, \fBTwoPhaseModel\fP< dim > & relperm)"

.PP
Incompressible Two Phase Flow Equation\&. first-order scheme for two phase flow ( linearazed form ): as in reference documentation

.PP
Computes all the terms necessary to solve in the saturation equation\&.

.PP
The gravitational segregation of the phases is taken care via 
.br
 the second term in:

.PP
dfds vt - d lambda_overbar / ds k (rho1 - rho2) g

.PP
This requires the analytically found derivative of the lambda overbar function\&. 
.br
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
All flow properties are computed at the element barycenter\&. 
.br

.PP
Capillary spreading is modelled with the FEM, so it is not included here\&. 
.br

.PP
MAYBE FACET INTEGRATION POINT INTERPOLATION WORKS BETTER in multidimensional case:

.PP
.PP
.nf
relperm\&.InitializeForFacetIntegrationPoint( i, 0U, pmem_, e );  
relperm\&.EffectiveSaturation(); 
facet_flux_[i] = param\&.FacetNormalVelocity(i) * param\&.FacetArea(i) * relperm\&.dfds();
.fi
.PP
 
