.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::StencilProcessor\fP< dim >::InitializeAdvectedVariableValues (const \fBElement\fP< dim > & e)"

.PP
second-order in time scheme for advection-diffusion equation: advected variable values at nodes and interpolated to facets Like 'Initialize()' but without the calculation of the facet fluxes\&. Depending on whether bijective mapping is used or not either variable is interpolated to the facet integration points\&. 
.br
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The FACETFLUXES at time-level t+dt are used to find the upstream saturation values\&. 
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
This method is used in the non-linear iteration loops to avoid unnecessary floating point operations\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::StencilProcessor\fP< dim >::InitializeFirstOrder (const \fBFV_Parameter\fP & param, const \fBElement\fP< dim > & e, const \fBVARIABLE_TYPE\fP & vt = \fRSCALAR\fP, uint32_t var_comp_nr = \fR0\fP)"

.PP
Advection Diffusion Equation\&. first-order scheme for advection-diffusion equation: sector volumes, advected variable values, and facet fluxes

.PP
Initializes sector pore volume and facet flux vectors for current finite element = finite volume stencil\&. 
.br
 It is implied that advected variable and nodal source are always of the same type (both SCALAR, both ARRAY or both FLAGGEDARRAY ) 
